<!--
    GH-1282: "8051: Decompiling the simplest code."
    https://github.com/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra/issues/1282
    Ported from kuna's tests/stages/gh1282-boolsignshift.xml (GayHydra #477).

    Source (Keil, opt off):
      byte xdata _buf[0x80];
      void Fn1() { byte i; for (i=0; i<0x80; i++) _buf[i] = 0; }

    8051 models the SUBB borrow / CY flag as bit 7 of PSW, so the loop bound
    `i < 0x80` is lowered to `((i < 0x80) << 7) s>> 7` (boolean shifted into the
    sign position and arithmetically shifted back = a 0/-1 sign-extended mask).
    Stock RuleLeftRight (ruleaction.cc) cancels `(V << c) s>> c` only when c is a
    multiple of 8, so for the boolean case (c == 7) the shift-by-7 carry noise
    survives all the way into the rendered C:

      while (uVar1 = 0x80 - (((uVar2 < 0x80) << 7LL) >> 7LL), 0x80 < uVar1) {

    "option booleanmask on|off" (default off = stock output) enables the new
    RuleBoolSignShift (ruleaction.cc, "analysis" group, right after RuleLeftRight)
    which recognizes `(b << k) s>> k` with NZMask(b) fitting in the low
    (width*8 - k) bits and rewrites it to the sign-extended-mask form `0 - b`
    (INT_2COMP), which the compare rules then clean to a plain boolean:

      for (uVar2 = 0; uVar1 = (uVar2 < 0x80) + 0x80, 0x80 < uVar1; uVar2 = uVar2 + 1) {

    Pass 1 (default pipeline, option off) reproduces the bug: assert #1 sees the
    `<< 7LL) >> 7LL` shift noise exactly once (present in pass 1, gone in pass 2).
    Pass 2 (after option booleanmask on) shows the folded bound: assert #2 sees
    `uVar1 = (uVar2 < 0x80) + 0x80` exactly once.

    kuna ships the fix default-on and its script toggles the option OFF for the
    second pass; the fork keeps stock output by default, so the passes are
    swapped (default first, then "option booleanmask on").  kuna's regexes name
    the variables v1/v2 and print the shift constant as plain 7; the fork prints
    uVar1/uVar2 and 7LL, so the names are loosened to \w+ and the LL suffix added.

    Disassembly:
      0000 e4        CLR  A
      0001 ff        MOV  R7,A
      0002 ef        MOV  A,R7
      0003 c3        CLR  CY
      0004 94 80     SUBB A,#0x80
      0006 74 80     MOV  A,#0x80
      0008 94 80     SUBB A,#0x80
      000a 50 0f     JNC  LAB_001b
      000c 74 00     MOV  A,#0x0
      000e 2f        ADD  A,R7
      000f f5 82     MOV  DPL,A
      0011 e4        CLR  A
      0012 34 00     ADDC A,#0x0
      0014 f5 83     MOV  DPH,A
      0016 e4        CLR  A
      0017 f0        MOVX @DPTR,A
      0018 0f        INC  R7
      0019 80 e7     SJMP LAB_0002
      001b 22        RET
